 ### Remaining bounded gap
 
 A short default lesson can still omit an object symmetric on both axes, so a left-right-first precedence rival may survive some three-example draws. That schedule-level teaching gap was not folded into this 15% connectivity repair.
+
+## 2026-10-24 review-e702987a9fcd90e6 — bounded lesson ambiguity audit
+
+Two executable alternatives fit all four visible demonstrations in a bounded consecutive-index lesson yet change its query:
+
+- Seed 11: treating a both-axis-symmetric object as left-right-only fits the four demonstrations and changes 20 query cells. The query is the first `precedence_both` profile in that five-pair window.
+- Seed 38: segmenting same-color objects with 4-connectivity fits the four demonstrations and changes 8 query cells, despite the generator's broader support for diagonal 8-connected witnesses elsewhere.
+
+All ten canonical labels were freshly replayed through protected Racket. This is a lesson-selection finding, not evidence that the canonical rule or Python mirror is mislabeled. No peer source repair was applied. A concrete next repair is to add both alternatives as executable lesson competitors and constructively require a both-axis precedence witness plus a diagonal-only 8-connected witness in every supported demonstration window before falling back to random profile draws.
+
+Evidence: `counterexamples/review-e702987a9fcd90e6-v0001/audit_assets.json` and `checks/peer-audits/9c5259babb4b.json`. The peer task suite remained green (66 passed); integration remains owner-selected and unverified as a repair.
